      "doctor_question": "Hello, I’m Dr. ____. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Well, hello Doctor. I came in today because... honestly, I just feel like I cannot settle inside my own skin anymore. It’s this constant feeling like I have to jump up and do the next thing, even when I am just completely worn out and really should be sitting still. \n\nBut sitting still is... well, it reminds me of when my sister tried to make me sit through that awful play down at the community theater last month. The seats were so stiff, and she bought the tickets for my birthday, so I couldn't just get up and leave. We drove her Buick there, the one with the broken air conditioning. It was absolutely sweltering. She refuses to get it fixed because her mechanic retired in, oh, it must have been 2018. \n\nBut anyway, even in my own house, in my comfortable chair, I just can't rest. I’m exhausted, but my body just wants to go. I don't even know how my sister sits through those long plays. Do you go to the theater much?",
