    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "When you need to focus on something, do you often have trouble keeping your attention on it?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S002",
      "patient_response": "Well, yes, actually. I mean, I try to focus. I'll sit down with the senior center newsletter, or maybe the choir schedule—oh, I sing alto in the community choir, have for years. Our director, Mrs. Higgins, she’s a lovely woman, but she insists on these incredibly complicated arrangements. Last Christmas we did this piece that had us switching time signatures every other measure. It was exhausting. And her husband, bless his heart, he tries to help by handing out the sheet music, but he always gets the pages mixed up. \n\nBut anyway, what was I saying? Oh, right, focusing. So I'll sit down with the newsletter or the schedule, and I start out just fine. But then, after a few minutes, I realize my eyes have just been going over the same lines again and again, and I have absolutely no idea what I just read. It's like my brain just went on a little vacation without telling me. Have you ever been to Florida? My cousin went there last winter and said the humidity was just unbearable.",
